        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c9d199cd-f777-3c55-ab6a-5988d25b620c",
                "word": "zircon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "18e6107b-f834-47f9-bd82-29faad08eec2",
                        "entry_id": "c9d199cd-f777-3c55-ab6a-5988d25b620c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "zircons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5246c2fb-a646-3ff4-b1b6-ea36457d85d9",
                        "entry_id": "c9d199cd-f777-3c55-ab6a-5988d25b620c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Espèce minérale du groupe des silicates sous groupe des nésosilicates de formule ZrSiO₄. Employé en bijouterie, dont les variétés incolores peuvent donner l’illusion du diamant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eeae2198-269b-441c-bda4-72e735a4b281",
                                "sense_id": "5246c2fb-a646-3ff4-b1b6-ea36457d85d9",
                                "text": "Bien qu’Octave ne cracherait pas là, tout de suite, sur la découverte d’un filon de wolframite ou de zircon, ou même sur le fait de traverser, à défaut d’y pouvoir poser le pied, ce que l’on nomme les « terres rares », histoire d’assurer la gratification et d’envisager les trois cent prochains jours avec sérénité. — (Robert Darvel, L’Homme qui traversa la Terre, Les Moutons électriques, 2016, page 87.)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52fd8e68-cd18-4a04-a9f4-470186adc5f9",
                                "sense_id": "5246c2fb-a646-3ff4-b1b6-ea36457d85d9",
                                "text": "Une fois formé, un cristal de zircon est si robuste qu’il résiste même si la roche-mère où il est inséré est exposée aux éléments (vent, pluie, etc.) assez longtemps pour qu'ils la détruisent complètement."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4f5d66d-b880-4ae8-aba2-4e9e1a1ddc5b",
                        "source_entry_id": "c9d199cd-f777-3c55-ab6a-5988d25b620c",
                        "source_sense_id": "5246c2fb-a646-3ff4-b1b6-ea36457d85d9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zirkon",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zirkon",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f47729c0-ad7e-3645-8b4c-d3fef9137d29",
                                        "entry_id": "4c5affdf-1eba-3d1b-a269-2e0daecf2019",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ein natürlicher Edelstein (Zirkonium-Silicat), im Unterschied zum synthetischen Diamant-Ersatz Zirkonia"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86ed2782-6c01-45e6-ad7c-fd90a96ead12",
                                                "sense_id": "f47729c0-ad7e-3645-8b4c-d3fef9137d29",
                                                "text": "Die bisher ältesten Minerale, die auf der Erde gefunden wurden, sind Zirkone aus [..] Westaustralien, mit einem Alter von 4,404 Milliarden Jahren."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5457abb5-6443-4569-a4c5-e3df376f8d72",
                        "source_entry_id": "c9d199cd-f777-3c55-ab6a-5988d25b620c",
                        "source_sense_id": "5246c2fb-a646-3ff4-b1b6-ea36457d85d9",
                        "target_lang_word": "zircon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "zircon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3d1251c-d408-3e25-9f74-a809d91f0cfb",
                                        "entry_id": "262e7c3d-97b9-38fc-a34c-0d2f4abb58c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mineral occurring in tetragonal crystals, usually of a brown or grey colour and consisting of silica and zirconia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f793055-2f6b-4a0d-9296-c2c51bd4bebd",
                                                "sense_id": "a3d1251c-d408-3e25-9f74-a809d91f0cfb",
                                                "text": "[…] salamanders, mermaids, chimaeras, wild men o’ the woods, leviathans, all hewn from faultless gems, thrice the bulk of a big man’s body, velvet-dark sapphires, chrysolite, beryl, amethyst, and the yellow zircon that is like transparent gold."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbd055f0-84a8-48ae-bb1c-fb7fcdc386bb",
                                                "sense_id": "a3d1251c-d408-3e25-9f74-a809d91f0cfb",
                                                "text": "Although there are dozens of different types of gems, among the best known and most important are […]. (Common gem materials not addressed in this article include amber, amethyst, chalcedony, garnet, lazurite, malachite, opals, peridot, rhodonite, spinel, tourmaline, turquoise and zircon.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "159b8417-ea34-308a-8f4e-2bf0c59fa78c",
                                        "entry_id": "262e7c3d-97b9-38fc-a34c-0d2f4abb58c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crystal of zircon, sometimes used as a false gemstone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21cdcc95-867d-46d6-914f-9e2fd39521a5",
                                                "sense_id": "159b8417-ea34-308a-8f4e-2bf0c59fa78c",
                                                "text": "A zircon princess, seemed to lost her senses"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f216009f-b2b7-4b19-a84a-7aad00453c95",
                        "source_entry_id": "c9d199cd-f777-3c55-ab6a-5988d25b620c",
